condition_name: Antiphospholipid Syndrome
condition_slug: antiphospholipid-syndrome
source: NSTG 2022
introduction: "A hyper coagulable disorder manifesting as recurrent venous and arterial thrombosis. Results in adverse effects in pregnancy. Associated with heterogeneous antibodies, anti-cardiolipin antibodies. Anti-B glycoprotein 1 antibodies and lupus anticoagulant. Commonly seen in young females of reproductive age. It may occur in 1-6% of the general population. It may be primary (with no associated disease) or secondary (associated with another systemic disease such as Systemic lupus erythematosus."
clinical_features[11]:
  - type: Venous thrombosis
    features[2]: Deep venous thrombosis,Pulmonary Embolism
  - type: Arterial thrombosis
    features[0]:
  - type: Pregnancy loss
    features[1]: 8%
  - type: Thrombocytopenia
    features[1]: 22%
  - type: Cutaneous
    features[4]: Livedo reticularis,Splinter haemorrhage,Superficial thrombophlebitis,Raynaud phenomenon
  - type: Neurologic
    features[4]: Cerebrovascular accident,Transient ischaemic attack,Migraines,Multi infarct dementia
  - type: Renal
    features[3]: Renal artery/vein thrombosis,Hypertension,Glomerular thrombosis
  - type: Pregnancy morbidities
    features[6]: Eclampsia/pre eclampsia,Intrauterine growth retardation,Small for age birth,Three or more unexplained recurrent,Consecutive pregnancy losses before 10 weeks cyesis,Any unexplained pregnancy loss after 10 weeks cyesis
  - type: HELLP syndrome
    features[1]: "Haemolysis, Elevated liver enzymes, and Low platelet count"
  - type: Pulmonary
    features[2]: Pulmonary embolism,Pulmonary hypertension
  - type: Other
    features[2]: Valvular heart disease,Renal thrombotic microangiopathy
investigations[9]: FBC and ESR,"Serology: Anti-B2 glycoprotein antibodies IgG, IgM, IgA","Anti-cardiolipin antibodies(aCL) IgG, IgM, IgA",Lupus anticoagulant(LAC),Antinuclear antibody(ANA),"Antibodies to phospholipids( many are not yet in clinical use) eg phosphatidylserine, phosphatidic acid, phosphatidylinositol","ECHO, Doppler US scan",CT angiogram,Brain CT scan
treatment:
  goals[0]:
  non_drug[4]: Smoking cessation,Avoidance of supplemental oestrogen,Control of hypertension,Close monitoring during pregnancy
  drug[14]: Low dose aspirin 75 mg - 325 mg daily,Tabs hydroxychloroquine 200 mg - 400 mg daily,"For venous events: Unfractionated heparin or low molecular weight heparin (e.g enoxaparin 20 - 80 mg/dL subcutaneously every 12 hours)",Tabs warfarin INR target 2 - 3 if single event; INR 3 - 4 if recurrent venous thrombosis. NOT TO BE USED IN PREGNANCY because of teratogenicity,Factor Xa inhibitors (e.g. rivaroxaban 15 mg twice daily for three weeks and then 20 mg daily to prevent recurrence),"For arterial event: Tabs warfarin, INR target (2 - 3) at moderate (3 - 4) at high","Pregnancy morbidity prevention: Tabs aspirin 75 - 150 mg daily, Unfractionated or low molecular weight heparin (e.g enoxaparin 20 - 80 mg/dL subcutaneously every 12 hours depending on aPL titre",Tabs hydroxychloroquine 200 mg daily,"Catastrophic APS (CAPS): IV heparin for 7 - 10 days",IV Pulse methylprednisolone 500 - 1000 mg daily for 3 days,IV immune globulins 0.4 g/kg body weight for 4-5 days,Plasmapheresis,IV cyclophosphamide 500 - 750 mg/m2,IV rituximab 500 mg - 1 g day 1 and day 15
  adverse_reactions_and_cautions[0]:
  supportive_measures[0]:
differential_diagnoses[5]: Thrombosis from Protein C and S deficiency,Antithrombin III deficiency,Factor V Leiden mutation,Malignancy (Lymphoproliferative disorder),Thrombotic thrombocytopenic purpura
